[node name="IntroductionLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="MasterScroll/PageVBox/ContentArea/HBoxContainer/Control2"]
unique_name_in_owner = true
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
bbcode_enabled = true
fit_content = true
scroll_active = false
autowrap_mode = 2
text = "[font_size=24][color=#dff5ff]Introduction[/color][/font_size]\n\nNULL NETWORK began as an ambitious experiment assembled from abandoned code and maintained by volunteers. The application remains functional through community effort rather than official support.\n\nIts systems are intentionally obscure. Players document discoveries, debate mechanics and share field reports through NULL CHANNEL. Some information is useful. Some is outdated. Some is deliberately false.\n\nFor those still connected, NULL NETWORK is more than an application. It is a place for minds that do not fit elsewhere.\n\n[color=#65cfa0]Proceed at your own discretion.[/color]"

[node name="GetStartedLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="MasterScroll/PageVBox/ContentArea/HBoxContainer/Control2"]
unique_name_in_owner = true
visible = false
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
bbcode_enabled = true
fit_content = true
scroll_active = false
autowrap_mode = 2
text = "[font_size=24][color=#dff5ff]Get Started[/color][/font_size]\n\n[b]1. Create an operator account[/b]\nChoose your identity carefully. Your username becomes your public identity in NULL CHANNEL.\n\n[b]2. Choose one partner APK[/b]\nAn operator maintains one active partner at a time. Your partner grows through combat, affinity and your personal Tendencies.\n\n[b]3. Understand APKs and EXEs[/b]\nAPKs are stable digital partners. EXEs are corrupted or autonomous entities encountered during exploration.\n\n[b]4. Fight through Modules[/b]\nCombat uses equipped Modules rather than a generic attack command. Modules consume Stability and execute in a visible cycle.\n\n[b]5. Resolve defeated EXEs[/b]\n[color=#7fd9a8]PURIFY[/color] restores corrupted data. [color=#7fc9ff]TAME[/color] replaces your current partner. [color=#ff9d7f]CONSUME[/color] destroys the target for greater growth.\n\n[b]6. Read the community[/b]\nThe forum often mentions dangerous locations, hidden mechanics and unusual encounters before the game explains them."

[node name="GlossaryLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="MasterScroll/PageVBox/ContentArea/HBoxContainer/Control2"]
unique_name_in_owner = true
visible = false
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
bbcode_enabled = true
fit_content = true
scroll_active = false
autowrap_mode = 2
text = "[font_size=24][color=#dff5ff]Glossary[/color][/font_size]\n\n[b]ADMINISTRATOR[/b]\nA player who controls a majority of an area's Data Centers.\n\n[b]AGGRO LOCK[/b]\nA state where an operator cannot safely disengage from a pursuing entity.\n\n[b]BLACKHAT[/b]\nAn umbrella term for exploitative playstyles involving consumption, player killing, hacking or EXE taming.\n\n[b]DATA CENTER[/b]\nA fixed stronghold guarded by powerful programs. Unlike temporary dungeons, Data Centers persist.\n\n[b]DEAD ZONE[/b]\nA region with no active operators. These areas often contain unusual and dangerous ecosystems.\n\n[b]DOOM ZONE[/b]\nA region inhabited by only one active operator.\n\n[b]INDEX[/b]\nThe act of gathering and mapping information about an area.\n\n[b]WHITEHAT[/b]\nA purification-focused philosophy that rejects exploitative or corrupted systems."
